# trap-bare-return.allowlist — ADJUDICATED-BENIGN sites for
# monitor/watcher/trap-bare-return-lint.sh (your-org/nexus-code#1513).
#
# A row records a bare `return` in a function the lint's static walk REACHES
# from a trap handler, whose status a human has established NO caller consumes
# — so the wrong status a trap-time `return` reports (bash return.def: the
# status of the last command BEFORE the trap fired, not of the test above it)
# decides nothing. The reason must say WHERE the status is dropped: which call
# site ignores it, or that the function is the handler itself (an EXIT/signal
# handler's own status is discarded by bash).
#
# Columns (TAB-separated): <repo-relative path>	<function>	<reason>
# The reason is REQUIRED; a row without one is a REFUSAL (exit 3), not a pass.
#
# BOTH DIRECTIONS RED. A reachable bare return with no row reddens the lint;
# a row with no reachable bare return at that path/function is STALE and
# reddens it too — the function was fixed, renamed, or the walk no longer
# reaches it — so this list keeps describing the tree instead of accreting.
# The fix is always preferable to a row: `return 0` / `return 1` explicitly,
# or `return $?` immediately after the deciding command.
#
# Census at 8d0cff30 (bash monitor/watcher/trap-bare-return-lint.sh): 92
# functions in the tracked shell corpus hold a bare return; the walk reaches
# NONE of them, so this list is empty. Before adding a row, prefer the fix.
